From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: mm-optimize-put_mems_allowed-usage-fix

restore slub.c:get_any_partial() comment

Cc: Christoph Lameter <cl@linux.com>
Cc: David Rientjes <rientjes@google.com>
Cc: Mel Gorman <mgorman@suse.de>
Cc: Miao Xie <miaox@cn.fujitsu.com>
Cc: Peter Zijlstra <a.p.zijlstra@chello.nl>
Cc: Tejun Heo <tj@kernel.org>
Cc: Pekka Enberg <penberg@cs.helsinki.fi>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---

 mm/slub.c |   10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff -puN mm/slub.c~mm-optimize-put_mems_allowed-usage-fix mm/slub.c
--- a/mm/slub.c~mm-optimize-put_mems_allowed-usage-fix
+++ a/mm/slub.c
@@ -1624,8 +1624,16 @@ static struct page *get_any_partial(stru
 			if (n && cpuset_zone_allowed_hardwall(zone, flags) &&
 					n->nr_partial > s->min_partial) {
 				object = get_partial_node(s, n, c);
-				if (object)
+				if (object) {
+					/*
+					 * Don't check read_mems_allowed_retry()
+					 * here - if mems_allowed was updated in
+					 * parallel, that was a harmless race
+					 * between allocation and the cpuset
+					 * update
+					 */
 					return object;
+				}
 			}
 		}
 	} while (read_mems_allowed_retry(cpuset_mems_cookie));
_

